    "body": "Hardens publish-with-payment recovery for payment methods that redirect the browser through Stripe.\n\n- returns Stripe to a publication-specific authenticated route instead of generic `/jobs/new`\n- strips Stripe return query parameters from the address bar immediately, including client-secret-bearing parameters\n- fetches and polls the exact publication from the backend\n- treats `redirect_status` only as UX guidance; signed backend settlement remains the sole authority for money and publication\n- resumes failed payments safely and avoids accidentally selecting another pending publication\n- documents the recovery/security contract\n\nNo Flyway/backend schema change is required. Existing server-side publication idempotency, signed webhook settlement, ledger checks and escrow invariants remain unchanged.\n\nDo not merge until all latest-head required checks are green.",
